@startuml
title The numeric tower: eight carriers, twelve declared casts, eight auto-injected promotions

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "**Bool**\n`![bool]`\nliteral `true` `false` `yeap` `nope`" as BOOL #FEF3C7
rectangle "**Int**\n`![i32]`\nliteral `-?<digits>(i32)?`" as INT #DBEAFE
rectangle "**UInt32**\n`![u32]`\nliteral `<digits>u32`" as U32 #DBEAFE
rectangle "**Fixed**\n`![CanonicalFixedPoint]`\nliteral `-?<digits>p<scale>`" as FIX #DCFCE7
rectangle "**Float**\n`![f64]`\nliteral `-?<d>.<d>(e±<d>)?(f64)?`" as FLT #DCFCE7
rectangle "**BigInt**\n`![CanonicalBigInt]`\nliteral `-?<digits>n`\n+ unsuffixed <latex>i32</latex> overflow" as BIG #EDE9FE
rectangle "**BigRat**\n`![CanonicalBigRat]`\nliteral `<d>r` or `<d>r/<d>r`\n**the top of the lattice**" as RAT #FCE7F3
rectangle "**Str**\n`![str]`\nliteral `\" … \"`\n**no lossless target**" as STR #E0E7FF

rectangle "**Proc**\nthe one ALGEBRAIC sort — the\nunion carrier for collections\n(`ProcInt`, `ProcBigRat`, …)" as PROC #F3F4F6

BOOL -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> U32   : **auto** `BoolToUInt32`
BOOL -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> BIG   : **auto** `BoolToBigInt`
BOOL -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> RAT   : **auto** `BoolToBigRat`
U32  -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> BIG   : **auto** `UInt32ToBigInt`
U32  -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> RAT   : **auto** `UInt32ToBigRat`
FLT  -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> RAT   : **auto** `FloatToBigRat`
FIX  -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> RAT   : **auto** `FixedToBigRat`
BIG  -[#16A34A,thickness=2]-> RAT   : **auto** `BigIntToBigRat`

INT  -[#2563EB,thickness=2]-> BIG   : **declared** `IntToBigInt`
INT  -[#2563EB,thickness=2]-> RAT   : **declared** `IntToBigRat`

BOOL -[#DB2777,dashed]-> INT  : `int(a)` **BoolToInt**
FLT  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> INT  : `int(a)` **FloatToInt**
STR  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> INT  : `int(a)` **StrToInt**
INT  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> FLT  : `float(a)` **IntToFloat**
BOOL -[#DB2777,dashed]-> FLT  : `float(a)` **BoolToFloat**
STR  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> FLT  : `float(a)` **StrToFloat**
INT  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> STR  : `str(a)` **IntToStr**
BOOL -[#DB2777,dashed]-> STR  : `str(a)` **BoolToStr**
FLT  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> STR  : `str(a)` **FloatToStr**
INT  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> BOOL : `bool(a)` **IntToBool**
FLT  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> BOOL : `bool(a)` **FloatToBool**
STR  -[#DB2777,dashed]-> BOOL : `bool(a)` **StrToBool**

PROC -[#7C3AED,dotted]-> INT  : `int(a, m)` **IntBin**
PROC -[#7C3AED,dotted]-> U32  : `uint(a, m)` **UIntBin**
PROC -[#7C3AED,dotted]-> FLT  : `float(a, m)` **FloatBin**
PROC -[#7C3AED,dotted]-> FIX  : `fixed(a, m)` **FixedBin**
PROC -[#7C3AED,dotted]-> BIG  : `bigint(a)` **BigintCast**
PROC -[#7C3AED,dotted]-> RAT  : `bigrat(a)` **BigratCast**

note bottom of RAT
  Every lossless edge terminates at `BigRat`
  (<latex>\mathbb{Z} \subset \mathbb{Q}</latex> and the dyadic-scaled fixed-point
  values <latex>\subset \mathbb{Q}</latex>), which is why the
  round-trip property is stated there and
  why <latex>\mathrm{display}</latex> is not injective there.
end note

note bottom of PROC
  `Proc` is the DOMAIN of the width-bearing
  casts and the element type of `List`, `Bag`
  and `Map`. It has no literal of its own —
  every value enters through a `Proc<X>`
  injection.
end note

legend right
|= Edge style | = Kind | = Surface | = Emitted by |
|<#DCFCE7> solid green | lossless auto-injection | **none** (transparent) | `ast/src/auto_inject.rs` |
|<#DBEAFE> solid blue | declared injection | **none** (transparent) | `calculator.rs:252-253` |
|<#FCE7F3> dashed pink | declared unary cast | `int(a)` / `float(a)` / `str(a)` / `bool(a)` | `calculator.rs:354-369` |
|<#EDE9FE> dotted purple | numeric cast (width-bearing or unary) | `int(a, m)` … `bigrat(a)` | `calculator.rs:501-518` |
endlegend

